= Senator Bail Antilles of Alderaan

Alderaan’s senior senator is patient, precise and deeply attached to the procedures of the Ruusan constitution. He believes the Republic can be saved by people who know how the Senate actually works.

[? if advisor_action_timer > 0 : *Our advisors can act again in [+ advisor_action_timer +] turn(s).* ?]

- @antilles_concord: Broker a concord with the Core Moderates.
- @antilles_discipline: Call the Caucus to order.
- @antilles_procedure: Use the Senate rules against our opponents.
- @antilles_bureau: Old procedural friendships.
- @go_back: Back.

@antilles_concord
subtitle: +8 relations with the Core Moderates, +3 with the Independents.
choose-if: advisor_action_timer <= 0
unavailable-subtitle: Our advisors have already acted recently.
on-arrival: mod_relation += 8; ind_relation += 3; advisor_action_timer = 5

Over a long lunch in the Senate dining hall, Antilles reminds the Core Moderates how much they have in common with the Caucus.

@antilles_discipline
subtitle: Reduces dissent in every faction.
choose-if: advisor_action_timer <= 0
unavailable-subtitle: Our advisors have already acted recently.
on-arrival: inst_dissent -= 8; rimward_dissent -= 5; pacifist_dissent -= 5; hawk_dissent -= 5; advisor_action_timer = 5

Antilles reminds the Caucus, politely and at length, that a divided opposition is no opposition at all.

@antilles_procedure
subtitle: +1 political capital; calms the coalition if we are in government.
choose-if: advisor_action_timer <= 0
unavailable-subtitle: Our advisors have already acted recently.
on-arrival: capital += 1; coalition_dissent -= 1 if rc_in_govt; advisor_action_timer = 5

Antilles knows the Senate rulebook better than its authors did. A well-timed point of order buys the Caucus a favour or two.

@antilles_bureau
subtitle: Warms the Senate bureaucracy towards us a little.
choose-if: advisor_action_timer <= 0
unavailable-subtitle: Our advisors have already acted recently.
on-arrival: bureau_relation += 6; advisor_action_timer = 5

Antilles has sat on more procedural committees than anyone alive. The clerks who serve them still take his calls.
